{"name":"Carpaccio","hex":"#e34234","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"carpaccio","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Thinly sliced raw beef or tuna, usually served as an appetizer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carpaccio"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carpaccio","blocks":[{"text":"Carpaccio is a dish of meat or fish, thinly sliced or pounded thin, and served raw, typically as an appetiser. It was invented in 1950 by Giuseppe Cipriani, founder of Harry's Bar in Venice, Italy, and popularised during the second half of the twentieth century. The beef was served with lemon, olive oil and white truffle or Parmesan cheese. Later, the term was extended to dishes containing other raw meats or fish, thinly sliced and served with lemon or vinegar, olive oil, salt and ground pepper."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Carpaccio_with_cheese_in_Warsaw.jpg/330px-Carpaccio_with_cheese_in_Warsaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carpaccio","wikidata":"Q840392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Carpaccio_Cipriani.jpg/500px-Carpaccio_Cipriani.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Carpaccio_Cipriani.jpg/1280px-Carpaccio_Cipriani.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Carpaccio_Cipriani.jpg/500px-Carpaccio_Cipriani.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carpaccio Cipriani, thin slices of raw beef drizzled in mayonnaise, served at Harry's Bar (Venice, 2024)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarpaccio_Cipriani.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Red and white01","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Red_and_